    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repo, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` field \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`.\n\nTwo changes, matching the existing pattern for derived owner fields:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` property (integer, 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, right after `customerCode`. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` helper that runs the standard Luhn algorithm over the digits of `customerCode` (returning `null` when the code is absent, consistent with `membershipNumber`'s legacy-owner handling).\n\nThe Luhn implementation mirrors the test's `luhn(...)` reference exactly (right-to-left, doubling every second digit starting from the last, subtracting 9 when >9, then `(10 - sum%10) % 10`). `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit` \u2014 passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
